definition: Docker is a platform which helps in creating similar environment for running application in different machine or multiple machines in an isolated forrmat.
  It actually creates a bundle of the application and its dependency and we cna run that smae application in a different environment

  properties:
  -----------
  1. It create isolated environment which has no dependency on the parent machine OS
  2. It is lightweight, takes very little space
  3. We can run the same application in a different environment without having dependecny on the version of the apps in the environment
  4. Follows a class and object principle having images as class which has the blueprint of the application and
  container as objects which is getting created having the application dependency

  Images and containers
  ---------------------
  Images: Image consists of the application blueprint example: when we create a ubuntu image it will create an ubuntu image separately
  
  Container: Container creates a total separate isolated environment having a definition and related filesystem where we can run and execute commands in an isolated environment
  Example: if we run the ubuntu image and write any linux command it will show the proposed result as per the code


initial codes mostly used
--------------------------
  run         Create and run a new container from an image
  exec        Execute a command in a running container
  ps          List containers
  build       Build an image from a Dockerfile
  bake        Build from a file
  pull        Download an image from a registry
  push        Upload an image to a registry
  images      List images
  login       Authenticate to a registry
  logout      Log out from a registry
  search      Search Docker Hub for images
  version     Show the Docker version information
  info        Display system-wide information
